      "text": "Ballantine was founded as a railroad station in 1896, named after homesteader E.P. Ballantine.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ballantine%2C_Montana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "At its peak in the early 1910s, Ballantine hosted a bank, three general stores, a hotel, and even a cheese factory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.mtmemory.org/nodes/view/127454",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Irrigation transformed the surrounding sagebrush into farms of sugar beets and alfalfa, reshaping the local landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
